 utility of income</article-title><source>CEP Discussion paper</source><year>2007</year><volume>784</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pomp</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Brouwer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Rutten</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>QALY-tijd, nieuwe medische technologie, kosteneffectiviteit en richtlijnen</article-title><source>CPB Werkdocument</source><year>2007</year><volume>152</volume></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rawlins</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Culyer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>National institute for clinical excellence and its value judgements</article-title><source>British Medical Journal</source><year>2004</year><volume>329</volume><fpage>224</fpage><lpage>227</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15271836</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.329.7459.224</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Laupacis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Feeny</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Detsky</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tugwell</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How attractive does a new technology have to be to warrant adoption and utilization? Tentative guidelines for using clinical and economic evaluations</article-title><source>Canadian Medical Association Journal</source><year>1992</year><volume>146</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>481</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1306034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-typ